      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Extra keyboard pages were an optimization for early phone screens where space was limited. VR is the exact opposite. We are literally surrounded by our display tech. There's no reason to optimize for space, but on the other hand, our input mechanism (laser pointer) is inferior to a phone screen, which makes toggling extra screens painful.\n\nSo, UX optimizations for a VR keyboard should be exactly opposite of a phone keyboard. It makes more sense to have a larger keyboard with more buttons to reduce flipping states as much as possible",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
